{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-343",
  "title": "Seed Prompt",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Seed Prompt"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Develop PocketFlow TikTok Generator, a backend+frontend workflow that creates Adult Swim–style TikTok video scripts from brand context. It should allow users to submit brand inputs and parameters, then generate a JSON composition (assets, timing, text), with download + API trigger. In this initial phase for this feature, let's call it \"Phase 1 — Integrated Workflow MVP,\" let's have dev-mode usage with seeded data and no auth flow."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "User Configuration"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I want one user in one category: 1 Internal Operator (dev-mode). Let's create three different sample projects (sample brands)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Board Structure"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let's have the standard Kanban columns for the status of each task, such as \"Queued\", \"Sourcing\", \"Composing\", \"Rendered\", \"Published\"."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Authentication"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "There will be no end-user authentication (dev-mode only) for this application as this is an internal MVP and uses only local API keys (.env) for Pexels and Gemini."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Task Card Features"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For each task in the UI for a task card, you should be able to:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "edit brand context and parameters (duration, clip count)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "generate and download JSON script (plan with timing/assets/text)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "view 5 video + 5 image asset refs (from Pexels)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "view 5 text blocks (≤6 chars each)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-16",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "see constraints check (14s total, 2.8s per clip)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "see logs/errors and rerun"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "User Flow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When you first launch PocketFlow TikTok Generator, it's going to open the \"Content Generation → TikTok Video\" workflow screen with a prefilled demo. No login; a dev-mode operator is assumed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When you click on a user, you go into the main view, which displays their recent runs and presets. When you click on a project, you open a project detail with saved presets, last JSON script, and asset history."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Board Interaction"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You're going to see the columns. You'll be able to create a run, move cards as states update (auto-progress), filter by project, and trigger \"Generate\" / \"Download JSON\" from the card."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Visual Indicators"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You will see clip counters, duration meter (14s target), text-length badges (≤6 chars), and error/warning chips so you can quickly confirm the recipe and spot failures."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Permission System"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You can create/edit your own runs and download scripts, but you can't publish or modify runs owned by other projects."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}